# /etc/pam.d/certauth-optional — OPTIONAL mode.
#
# Same module, looser policy: USB cert auth is `sufficient` — if it
# succeeds, accept and stop; if the token is absent or auth fails, fall
# through to whatever follows (typically pam_unix.so prompting for a
# password). Use this during phased rollouts where not every user has
# been issued a token yet.
#
# Account stays `required` (denial propagates) and session stays
# `required` so the registry/audit handlers run for every session.
#
# Switch to `certauth` (strict) once token coverage is universal.

auth        sufficient   pam_certauth.so
account     required     pam_certauth.so
session     required     pam_certauth.so
